!Series_summary	"Hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) affects millions of people worldwide and is a lethal malignancy for which there are no effective therapies. To identify prognostic gene markers for liver cancer, we conducted transcriptome profiling of frozen tissues (tumor and non-tumor) from 300 early-to-advanced stage HCCs plus 40 cirrhotic and 6 normal livers."
!Series_overall_design	"We have profiles 268 HCC tumor, 243 adjacent non-tumor, 40 cirrhotic and 6 healthy liver samples."
!Series_type	"Expression profiling by array"
!Series_contributor	"Chunsheng,,Zhang"
